---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { categories, findItem, menu } from '../lib/menu';
import { guidance } from '../data/menu-guidance';
import { url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Compare Pizza, Sandwiches, Maggi & Pasta | Bhuk Lagla Menu Guide"
  description="Compare Bhuk Lagla's actual toppings, fillings, sauces and seasonings. Choose among the vegetarian pizza, sandwiches, Maggi, pasta and fries in Sundargarh."
>
  <section class="wrap page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Follow your craving</p>
    <h1>
      What makes
      <br />
      each bite different?
    </h1>
    <p>A side-by-side guide to our menu’s toppings, fillings and sauces.</p>
    <p class="small-text">
      Published by Bhuk Lagla · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-17">17 October 2026</time>
    </p>
    <nav class="category-links" aria-label="Compare menu categories">
      {categories.map((category) => (
        <a class="button secondary" href={`#${category.id}`}>
          {category.name}
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap prose section">
    <h2>Choose in three steps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Pick the format: pizza, a grilled sandwich, a bowl of Maggi or pasta, or fries.</li>
      <li>Compare the listed ingredients below. Look for the topping or sauce you enjoy.</li>
      <li>
        Open the dish description, then confirm portion choices, availability and your total on
        Zomato.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      This guide compares our {menu.length} named dishes in {categories.length} website categories.
      Counts come from this website’s catalogue, not sales data. Taste notes summarise the public
      descriptions; they are not taste-test scores, popularity rankings or complete allergen lists.
    </p>
  </section>
  {categories.map((category) => (
    <section class="wrap comparison-section section" id={category.id}>
      <p class="eyebrow">
        {guidance[category.id].picks.length} dishes · {category.name}
      </p>
      <h2>{guidance[category.id].question}</h2>
      <p class="comparison-intro">{guidance[category.id].answer}</p>
      <div
        class="comparison-table"
        role="region"
        aria-label={`${category.name} ingredient comparison`}
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <table>
          <caption>{category.name}: differences in the listed ingredients</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Dish</th>
              <th scope="col">What makes it different</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {guidance[category.id].picks.map(([id, note]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  <a href={url(`menu/${id}/`)}>{findItem(id).name}</a>
                </th>
                <td>{note}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={url(`menu/category/${category.id}/`)}>
        Browse {category.name.toLowerCase()} images and dishes →
      </a>
    </section>
  ))}
  <section class="wrap prose section">
    <h2>Two ways to use this guide</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>If you want corn but are choosing a sauce:</strong> compare Corn Masti Pizza’s pizza
      sauce with Schezwan Corn Pizza’s spicy Schezwan sauce and red paprika. Corn Olive Pizza adds
      black olive instead. Open each description before choosing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>If you are planning food for an office gathering:</strong> shortlist the formats and
      fillings people want, then <a href={url('contact/?type=party')}>send a party enquiry</a> with
      the date and guest count. These are example decisions, not reports of completed customer
      events.
    </p>
    <p>
      Dietary restriction? <a href={url('answers/#allergies')}>Read the ingredient guidance</a> and
      ask the kitchen before ordering. For more about how we prepare this information, see{' '}
      <a href={url('content-standards/')}>sources and corrections</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
